  "@type": "DefinedTerm",
  "alternateName": "Contaminants level in wild seafood edible tissues below threshold values",
  "description": "The level of contaminants in edible tissues\n(muscle, liver, roe, flesh or other soft\nparts, as appropriate) of seafood (including fish, crustaceans, molluscs, echinoderms, seaweed and other marine plants)\ncaught or harvested in the wild (excluding\nfin-fish from mariculture) does not exceed:\n\n(a) for contaminants listed in Regulation\n(EC) No 1881/2006, the maximum\nlevels laid down in that Regulation,\nwhich are the threshold values for the\npurposes of this Decision;\n\n(b) for additional contaminants, not listed\nin Regulation (EC) No 1881/2006,\nthreshold values, which Member\nStates shall establish through regional\nor subregional cooperation.",
  "disambiguatingDescription": "This term was created by MBO WP1 task 1.3 with external domain experts during the MARCO-BOLO Project to express that this object is of relevance to the named criterion of the MFSD",
